<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="419074a1">&lt;p&gt;
    Analyze the test scenarios and prepare the criteria to create or obtain the required test data. The criteria provided
    should be as specific as possible to verify data accuracy.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    When performing this task,&amp;nbsp;consider the following:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        What data is needed?&amp;nbsp;
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        How much data is needed?
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        When is the data needed?
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Does the data need to be refreshed after a specified period of time?
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        In what test environment is the data needed?
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Are there any dependencies or integration points to address?
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Who will need the data?&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="6bf901a1"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="bc88fffb">&lt;p&gt;
    For large scale projects, data requirements may vary depending on several factors, such as the number of test
    environments, the test levels and types performed, or the size of the project team. In these situations, data
    requirements are collated, consolidated and reviewed with stakeholders. On smaller scale projects, in less formal
    settings, individual data requests may be submitted and fulfilled on an as need basis. In many cases, too much may
    increase cost and time associated to creating or obtaining data while an insufficient amount of data may impact test
    effectiveness.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="801f89d0"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="66158fc6">&lt;p&gt;
    To understand what data is needed to test that solution behavior aligns with user requirements.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
